.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt STRIP 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm strip
.Nd remove symbol and debug information from an ELF file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl g|s
.Op Fl o Ar outfile
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility removes unnecessary ELF32/ELF64 little-endian symbol and debug information.
By default it neutralizes the section headers of
.Dq .symtab ,
the
.Dq .strtab
table dedicated to it, and
.Dq .debug* ,
.Dq .zdebug* ,
.Dq .stab* ,
.Dq .line
sections.
.Pp
Section contents and program headers are not moved.
The section-header table stays at its original offset, so the entry point and every program
header remain valid and the stripped executable still runs.
.Dq .dynsym
and
.Dq .dynstr
are preserved.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl g
Remove debug sections only and keep
.Dq .symtab .
.It Fl s
Remove symbols, the dedicated string table and debug sections.
This is the default.
.It Fl o Ar outfile
Copy the input to
.Ar outfile ,
strip the copy and leave the input untouched.
Only one input file is accepted with this option.
.El
.Pp
Each section header is cleared in place and the result is reparsed and verified before it is
written.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A missing or malformed input exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ar 1 ,
.Xr nm 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the POSIX
.Nm
interface.
The
.Fl g ,
.Fl s
and
.Fl o
extensions follow the historical tool behaviour.
